# Keep the working copy byte-identical to what CI checks out. core.autocrlf gives a Windows working
# copy CRLF while the Linux runner checks out LF, so Spotless and Prettier, which read the working
# copy, fail locally on files that pass in CI, and any tool that rewrites a file with LF shows every
# line of it as changed. Pinning the ending here makes every clone agree, whatever its settings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# gradlew.bat is stored exactly as committed, with no conversion. cmd.exe misreads a batch file's
# labels and goto targets under LF, so it has to reach every working copy with CRLF, and it is
# committed with CRLF: Dependabot's wrapper bumps write it that way. Converting it, as
# `text eol=crlf` did, disagreed with those blobs, and every Windows clone showed it as modified.
*.bat -text
*.jar binary
